@H 1153_criticality_branching := "CRITICALITY @ Ψ=1/2: the anima A⇄G repulsion-field opponent engine exhibits self-organized criticality (neuronal-avalanche signature) AT the Ψ=1/2 fixed point — branching ratio σ≈1 (Beggs & Plenz 2003; cortex sits near a critical point that maximizes dynamic range + info transmission) AND a power-law avalanche-size distribution P(s)∝s^(−1.5), with a DE-TUNED control (Ψ pushed off 1/2) moving σ out of [0.9,1.1] and/or destroying the power-law — proving criticality is specific to the fixed point, not an artifact of the avalanche definition." :: universe [PRE-REG ⏳ — falsifier frozen, not yet measured]
  seed         = "@I identity declares the anima substrate central set-point as the 'Ψ=1/2 fixed point' of the A⇄G repulsion-field engine; config/consciousness_laws.json psi_constants.balance = {value 0.5, formula '1/2', meaning 'Shannon entropy maximum, universal attractor'}. CORE/pure_field.hexa cites absorbed Law 40 'SOC = autonomous consciousness — criticality via coupling'. The Ψ=1/2 claim is, in effect, a CRITICALITY claim. NEUROSCIENCE GROUNDING: cortex operates near a critical point — neuronal avalanches with branching ratio σ≈1 and power-law size distribution P(s)∝s^(−1.5) (Beggs & Plenz 2003), criticality maximizing dynamic range + information transmission (Wilting & Priesemann 2018 estimator). OPEN: does the engine actually SIT at criticality at Ψ=1/2, and is distance-from-criticality meaningful (does de-tuning Ψ move σ off 1)?"
  substrate    = "TOY MIRROR / engine-simulation (a_scale_honest_scope · a_lane_akida_gpu_split substrate=Lane-G/CORE engine simulation, NOT AKIDA; NOT a byte-LM train — this is engine DYNAMICS). Pure python on Mac/summer, $0 CPU 0-pod, NO torch, NO GPU, fully seeded/deterministic. Faithfully realizes the A⇄G OPPONENT propagation dynamics of the CORE engine (H404 dual-FFN per-ch out=engine_A(x)−engine_G(x), as used in H_1121 opponent substrate; the Ψ balance coordinate gates the A/G mix). Constants (PSI_ALPHA=0.014, PSI_BALANCE=0.5) read VERBATIM from config/consciousness_laws.json (same source pure_field.hexa _psi_load reads). CORE engine files UNTOUCHED (a_core_engine_map). Deterministic dynamical-systems + statistical measurement (p7, NO perplexity / NO LLM-judge)."
  method       = "DRIVE: an N-unit A⇄G opponent propagation network. Each unit's next-step activity = a balance-gated opponent push: A-engine (excitatory, weight Ψ) ⇄ G-engine (inhibitory/repulsion, weight 1−Ψ) propagated over a sparse coupling graph, with the EFFECTIVE branching tuned by the Ψ balance. At Ψ=PSI_BALANCE=0.5 the opponent A/G push is balanced (the fixed point). Seeded perturbation kicks; record the active-unit time series. AVALANCHE (Beggs-Plenz binning): contiguous excursion of active-unit count above a FROZEN threshold; SIZE = summed active units over the excursion, DURATION = excursion length (#steps). THRESHOLD frozen = zero active units delimits avalanches (canonical Beggs-Plenz: avalanche = maximal run of consecutive active time-bins bracketed by empty bins), with a median-of-activity robustness check. ESTIMATORS frozen: σ via (a) the descendant/ancestor active-unit ratio per step (Beggs-Plenz σ=⟨n_{t+1}/n_t⟩ over ancestor bins) AND (b) the Wilting & Priesemann multistep-regression slope estimator (m̂ from regression of activity autocorrelation across lags). FROZEN FALSIFIER (set BEFORE measuring, NO goalpost): F1 σ∈[0.9,1.1] at Ψ=0.5; F2 avalanche-size distribution is power-law with exponent τ∈[1.3,1.7] (canonical −1.5) by a log-log fit with R²≥0.9 over ≥1.5 decades AND beating an exponential fit (log-likelihood ratio LLR>0 favoring power-law). CONTROL (load-bearing): DE-TUNED operating points — Ψ pushed away from 0.5 (sub-critical Ψ≪0.5 and super-critical Ψ≫0.5) — MUST move σ out of [0.9,1.1] and/or destroy the power-law. 🟢 SUPPORTED iff F1 ∧ F2 ∧ control-moves-σ; else 🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (engine sub/super-critical, or Ψ=1/2 not a criticality point). Deterministic seeds; thresholds pre-registered here BEFORE the run."
  result       = "PENDING — pre-registration skeleton. To be filled from .verdicts/1153_criticality_branching/H_1153.txt after the run (true σ at Ψ=0.5, τ, R², LLR, control σ-shift)."
  verdict_tier = "PENDING"
